<h3 data-start=3D"1583" data-end=3D"1631">=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"1=
589" data-end=3D"1631">4. Handle Synonyms or Alternate Titles</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1632" data-end=3D"1754">Consider mapping popular nicknames=
 or alternate titles to official movie names. Example: "LOTR" =E2=86=92 "Th=
e Lord of the Rings".</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1756" data-end=3D"1846">
<li data-start=3D"1756" data-end=3D"1846">
<p data-start=3D"1758" data-end=3D"1846">You can maintain a small alias dic=
tionary for frequently mistyped or abbreviated titles.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1848" data-end=3D"1851">
<h3 data-start=3D"1853" data-end=3D"1910">=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"1=
859" data-end=3D"1910">5. Suggest Closest Matches (User Feedback Loop)</str=
ong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1911" data-end=3D"2014">If the system cannot find an exact=
 match, show the user a list of top 3 closest matches to choose from.</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"2016" data-end=3D"2048">
<p data-start=3D"2018" data-end=3D"2048"><em data-start=3D"2018" data-end=
