<h3 data-start=3D"1243" data-end=3D"1290">=E2=9C=85 Step 3: Double-Click th=
e Header or Footer</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1291" data-end=3D"1443">
<li data-start=3D"1291" data-end=3D"1363">
<p data-start=3D"1293" data-end=3D"1363">Scroll to the <strong data-start=
=3D"1307" data-end=3D"1344">section where you want to re-link</strong> the =
header/footer.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1364" data-end=3D"1443">
<p data-start=3D"1366" data-end=3D"1443"><strong data-start=3D"1366" data-e=
nd=3D"1382">Double-click</strong> inside the <strong data-start=3D"1394" da=
ta-end=3D"1419">header or footer area</strong> (top or bottom margin).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1445" data-end=3D"1494">This will activate the <strong dat=
a-start=3D"1468" data-end=3D"1493">Header &amp; Footer Tools</strong>.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1496" data-end=3D"1543">=E2=9C=85 Step 4: Use the "Link t=
o Previous" Button</h3>
<ol data-start=3D"1544" data-end=3D"1783">
<li data-start=3D"1544" data-end=3D"1632">
<p data-start=3D"1547" data-end=3D"1632">You=E2=80=99ll see a new tab: <str=
ong data-start=3D"1569" data-end=3D"1588">Header &amp; Footer</strong> (or =
<strong data-start=3D"1593" data-end=3D"1603">Design</strong>, depending on=
 Word version).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1633" data-end=3D"1705">
<p data-start=3D"1636" data-end=3D"1705">In the <strong data-start=3D"1643"=
 data-end=3D"1657">Navigation</strong> group, click the <strong data-start=
=3D"1675" data-end=3D"1697">=E2=80=9CLink to Previous=E2=80=9D</strong> but=
ton.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1706" data-end=3D"1783">
<p data-start=3D"1709" data-end=3D"1783">When <strong data-start=3D"1714" d=
ata-end=3D"1727">turned ON</strong>, the button becomes <strong data-start=
=3D"1748" data-end=3D"1763">highlighted</strong> (or stays pressed).</p>
</li>
</ol>
<blockquote data-start=3D"1785" data-end=3D"1885">
<p data-start=3D"1787" data-end=3D"1885">=F0=9F=93=8C <strong data-start=3D=
"1790" data-end=3D"1804">Important:</strong> You must do this separately fo=
r <strong data-start=3D"1837" data-end=3D"1860">headers and footers</strong=
> if you want both linked.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3 data-start=3D"1887" data-end=3D"1922">=E2=9C=85 Step 5: Save or Apply C=
hanges</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1923" data-end=3D"2089">
<li data-start=3D"1923" data-end=3D"2024">
<p data-start=3D"1925" data-end=3D"2024">Once linked, the current section w=
ill <strong data-start=3D"1963" data-end=3D"1999">mirror the header/footer =
content</strong> of the previous section.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2025" data-end=3D"2089">
<p data-start=3D"2027" data-end=3D"2089">Make any edits you want=E2=80=94th=
ey will now appear in both sections.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"2091" data-end=3D"2094">
<h2 data-start=3D"2096" data-end=3D"2137">=F0=9F=91=81=EF=B8=8F=E2=80=8D=F0=
=9F=97=A8=EF=B8=8F <strong data-start=3D"2107" data-end=3D"2137">To Check i=
f Linking Worked</strong></h2>
<ul data-start=3D"2139" data-end=3D"2261">
<li data-start=3D"2139" data-end=3D"2173">
<p data-start=3D"2141" data-end=3D"2173">Scroll between the two sections.</=
p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2174" data-end=3D"2261">
<p data-start=3D"2176" data-end=3D"2261">If both headers or footers look id=
entical and update together, linking is successful.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"2263" data-end=3D"2266">
<h2 data-start=3D"2268" data-end=3D"2290">=F0=9F=92=A1 Example Scenario</h2=
>
<p data-start=3D"2292" data-end=3D"2314">Say your document has:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2316" data-end=3D"2457">
<li data-start=3D"2316" data-end=3D"2383">
<p data-start=3D"2318" data-end=3D"2383"><strong data-start=3D"2318" data-e=
nd=3D"2331">Section 1</strong>: Roman numerals for Abstract, Acknowledgemen=
t, etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2384" data-end=3D"2457">
<p data-start=3D"2386" data-end=3D"2457"><strong data-start=3D"2386" data-e=
nd=3D"2399">Section 2</strong>: Arabic numbers for the main content (Introd=
uction, etc.)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2459" data-end=3D"2681">If you had <strong data-start=3D"2=
470" data-end=3D"2484">turned OFF</strong> "Link to Previous" in Section 2 =
to change number format, and now want the <strong data-start=3D"2559" data-=
end=3D"2586">same header/footer text</strong> (e.g., chapter title or your =
name) as Section 1, you can <strong data-start=3D"2644" data-end=3D"2655">t=
urn ON</strong> "Link to Previous" again.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2683" data-end=3D"2686">
<p data-start=3D"2688" data-end=3D"2722">Let me know if you need help with:=
</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2723" data-end=3D"2891" data-is-last-node=3D"" data-is-on=
ly-node=3D"">
<li data-start=3D"2723" data-end=3D"2773">
<p data-start=3D"2725" data-end=3D"2773">Managing <strong data-start=3D"273=
4" data-end=3D"2755">different headers</strong> on odd/even pages</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2774" data-end=3D"2822">
<p data-start=3D"2776" data-end=3D"2822">Creating a <strong data-start=3D"2=
787" data-end=3D"2822">title page without page numbers</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2823" data-end=3D"2891" data-is-last-node=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2825" data-end=3D"2891" data-is-last-node=3D"">Adjusting <=
strong data-start=3D"2835" data-end=3D"2860">page number positions</strong>=
