:prose-invert w-full break-words light markdown-new-styling"><p data-start=
=3D"0" data-end=3D"139">Thanks! Here's a <strong data-start=3D"17" data-end=
=3D"57">detailed guide specific to Word 2019</strong> on how to <strong dat=
a-start=3D"68" data-end=3D"98">turn ON "Link to Previous"</strong> for head=
ers or footers between sections.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"141" data-end=3D"144">
<h2 data-start=3D"146" data-end=3D"202">=F0=9F=94=81 How to Turn ON =E2=80=
=9CLink to Previous=E2=80=9D in <strong data-start=3D"189" data-end=3D"202"=
>Word 2019</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"204" data-end=3D"228">=F0=9F=93=9D <strong data-start=3D"=
211" data-end=3D"228">What it does:</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"229" data-end=3D"415">
<li data-start=3D"229" data-end=3D"336">
<p data-start=3D"231" data-end=3D"336">When <strong data-start=3D"236" data=
-end=3D"242">ON</strong>, the <strong data-start=3D"248" data-end=3D"265">h=
eader/footer</strong> in your current section will be <strong data-start=3D=
"298" data-end=3D"335">identical to the previous section</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"337" data-end=3D"415">
<p data-start=3D"339" data-end=3D"415">When <strong data-start=3D"344" data=
-end=3D"351">OFF</strong>, the current section can have its <strong data-st=
art=3D"386" data-end=3D"414">own unique header/footer</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"417" data-end=3D"420">
<h2 data-start=3D"422" data-end=3D"469">=E2=9C=85 Step-by-Step Instructions=
 in <strong data-start=3D"456" data-end=3D"469">Word 2019</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"471" data-end=3D"511">=F0=9F=94=B9 <strong data-start=3D"=
478" data-end=3D"511">Step 1: Open Header or Footer</strong></h3>
<ol data-start=3D"512" data-end=3D"746">
<li data-start=3D"512" data-end=3D"539">
<p data-start=3D"515" data-end=3D"539">Open your Word document.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"540" data-end=3D"603">
<p data-start=3D"543" data-end=3D"603">Scroll to the page where you want to=
 link the header/footer.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"604" data-end=3D"746">
<p data-start=3D"607" data-end=3D"698"><strong data-start=3D"607" data-end=
=3D"623">Double-click</strong> in the <strong data-start=3D"631" data-end=
=3D"641">header</strong> (top margin) or <strong data-start=3D"658" data-en=
d=3D"668">footer</strong> (bottom margin) of that page.</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"703" data-end=3D"746">
<p data-start=3D"705" data-end=3D"746">This opens the <strong data-start=3D=
"720" data-end=3D"745">Header &amp; Footer Tools</strong>.</p>
</blockquote>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"748" data-end=3D"751">
<h3 data-start=3D"753" data-end=3D"808">=F0=9F=94=B9 <strong data-start=3D"=
760" data-end=3D"808">Step 2: Locate the =E2=80=9CLink to Previous=E2=80=9D=
 Option</strong></h3>
<ol data-start=3D"809" data-end=3D"1121">
<li data-start=3D"809" data-end=3D"943">
<p data-start=3D"812" data-end=3D"943">At the top of Word, go to the <stron=
g data-start=3D"842" data-end=3D"876">Header &amp; Footer Tools =E2=80=93 D=
esign</strong> tab (which appears automatically when editing a header or fo=
oter).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"944" data-end=3D"980">
<p data-start=3D"947" data-end=3D"980">Look in the <strong data-start=3D"95=
9" data-end=3D"973">Navigation</strong> group.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"981" data-end=3D"1121">
<p data-start=3D"984" data-end=3D"1024">Click the button <strong data-start=
=3D"1001" data-end=3D"1024">=E2=80=9CLink to Previous.=E2=80=9D</strong></p=
>
<ul data-start=3D"1029" data-end=3D"1121">
<li data-start=3D"1029" data-end=3D"1070">
<p data-start=3D"1031" data-end=3D"1070">=E2=9C=85 If it's <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"1041" data-end=3D"1056">highlighted</strong>, it's <strong data-start=
=3D"1063" data-end=3D"1069">ON</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1074" data-end=3D"1121">
<p data-start=3D"1076" data-end=3D"1121">=F0=9F=94=B2 If it's <strong data-=
start=3D"1087" data-end=3D"1106">not highlighted</strong>, it's <strong dat=
a-start=3D"1113" data-end=3D"1120">OFF</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<blockquote data-start=3D"1123" data-end=3D"1206">
<p data-start=3D"1125" data-end=3D"1206">Clicking it will toggle the state.=
 To <strong data-start=3D"1163" data-end=3D"1177">turn it ON</strong>, make=
 sure it's highlighted.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr data-start=3D"1208" data-end=3D"1211">
<h3 data-start=3D"1213" data-end=3D"1272">=F0=9F=94=B9 <strong data-start=
=3D"1220" data-end=3D"1272">Step 3: Repeat for Header and Footer (If Needed=
)</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1273" data-end=3D"1482">
<li data-start=3D"1273" data-end=3D"1326">
<p data-start=3D"1275" data-end=3D"1326">Word treats <strong data-start=3D"=
1287" data-end=3D"1298">headers</strong> and <strong data-start=3D"1303" da=
ta-end=3D"1314">footers</strong> separately.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1327" data-end=3D"1482">
<p data-start=3D"1329" data-end=3D"1403">If you want both the header <stron=
g data-start=3D"1357" data-end=3D"1364">and</strong> footer linked to the p=
revious section:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1406" data-end=3D"1482">
<li data-start=3D"1406" data-end=3D"1482">
<p data-start=3D"1408" data-end=3D"1482">Double-click the <strong data-star=
t=3D"1425" data-end=3D"1440">footer area</strong> and turn on <strong data-=
start=3D"1453" data-end=3D"1475">"Link to Previous"</strong> again.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1484" data-end=3D"1487">
<h2 data-start=3D"1489" data-end=3D"1511">=F0=9F=93=8C Important Notes:</h2=
>
<ul data-start=3D"1512" data-end=3D"1765">
<li data-start=3D"1512" data-end=3D"1644">
<p data-start=3D"1514" data-end=3D"1644">"Link to Previous" works <strong d=
ata-start=3D"1539" data-end=3D"1558">within sections</strong>. You must hav=
e a <strong data-start=3D"1576" data-end=3D"1593">section break</strong> (n=
ot just a page break) for Word to allow linking.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1645" data-end=3D"1765">
<p data-start=3D"1647" data-end=3D"1765">If the content does <strong data-s=
tart=3D"1667" data-end=3D"1681">not update</strong> after linking, try <str=
ong data-start=3D"1701" data-end=3D"1730">copying the header/footer</strong=
> content from the previous section.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1767" data-end=3D"1770">
<h2 data-start=3D"1772" data-end=3D"1802">=F0=9F=8E=93 When Would You Use T=
his?</h2>
<ul data-start=3D"1803" data-end=3D"2041">
<li data-start=3D"1803" data-end=3D"1863">
<p data-start=3D"1805" data-end=3D"1863">Re-using the same page number form=
at in multiple sections.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1864" data-end=3D"1952">
<p data-start=3D"1866" data-end=3D"1952">Applying the same header/footer te=
xt (e.g., title, author, logo) to multiple sections.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1953" data-end=3D"2041">
<p data-start=3D"1955" data-end=3D"2041">After disabling it to use differen=
t headers and now wanting to return to uniform ones.</p>
</li>
</ul>
