-[3px]"><div class=3D"markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words l=
ight markdown-new-styling"><p data-start=3D"0" data-end=3D"148">If you want=
 to <strong data-start=3D"15" data-end=3D"53">remove or turn off a section =
break</strong> in Word 2019, here=E2=80=99s how to do it safely without mes=
sing up your formatting or page numbering:</p>
<hr data-start=3D"150" data-end=3D"153">
<h2 data-start=3D"155" data-end=3D"198">How to Remove (Turn Off) a Section =
Break</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"200" data-end=3D"233">Step 1: Show Formatting Marks</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"234" data-end=3D"349">
<li data-start=3D"234" data-end=3D"349">
<p data-start=3D"236" data-end=3D"349">Press <strong data-start=3D"242" dat=
a-end=3D"262">Ctrl + Shift + 8</strong> (or click the =C2=B6 symbol on the =
Home tab) to display paragraph marks and section breaks.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"351" data-end=3D"387">Step 2: Locate the Section Break</h=
3>
<ul data-start=3D"388" data-end=3D"488">
<li data-start=3D"388" data-end=3D"488">
<p data-start=3D"390" data-end=3D"488">Scroll through your document and fin=
d the <strong data-start=3D"432" data-end=3D"449">section break</strong> yo=
u want to remove. It will appear as:</p>
</li>
</ul>
<blockquote data-start=3D"490" data-end=3D"575">
<p data-start=3D"492" data-end=3D"575"><strong data-start=3D"492" data-end=
=3D"529">--- Section Break (Next Page) ---</strong><br data-start=3D"529" d=
ata-end=3D"532">
or <strong data-start=3D"537" data-end=3D"575">--- Section Break (Continuou=
s) ---</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<h3 data-start=3D"577" data-end=3D"613">Step 3: Delete the Section Break</h=
3>
<ul data-start=3D"614" data-end=3D"723">
<li data-start=3D"614" data-end=3D"661">
<p data-start=3D"616" data-end=3D"661">Click just <strong data-start=3D"627=
" data-end=3D"637">before</strong> the section break line.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"662" data-end=3D"723">
<p data-start=3D"664" data-end=3D"723">Press <strong data-start=3D"670" dat=
a-end=3D"680">Delete</strong> (or Backspace if your cursor is after it).</p=
>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"725" data-end=3D"728">
<h2 data-start=3D"730" data-end=3D"749">Important Notes:</h2>
<ul data-start=3D"751" data-end=3D"1123">
<li data-start=3D"751" data-end=3D"1003">
<p data-start=3D"753" data-end=3D"826"><strong data-start=3D"753" data-end=
=3D"821">Deleting a section break merges the sections before and after it</=
strong>, so:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"829" data-end=3D"1003">
<li data-start=3D"829" data-end=3D"908">
<p data-start=3D"831" data-end=3D"908">Page numbering, headers/footers, mar=
gins, and formatting may merge or change.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"911" data-end=3D"1003">
<p data-start=3D"913" data-end=3D"1003">You might need to <strong data-star=
t=3D"931" data-end=3D"966">reapply page numbering settings</strong> or head=
er/footer settings afterward.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1005" data-end=3D"1123">
<p data-start=3D"1007" data-end=3D"1123">If you want to <strong data-start=
=3D"1022" data-end=3D"1069">keep different page numbering or formatting</st=
rong> in each section, do <strong data-start=3D"1090" data-end=3D"1097">not=
</strong> delete the section break.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1125" data-end=3D"1128">
<h2 data-start=3D"1130" data-end=3D"1207">If You Want to Keep the Section B=
reak But Remove the Blank Page It Causes:</h2>
<p data-start=3D"1208" data-end=3D"1269">Sometimes a <strong data-start=3D"=
1220" data-end=3D"1247">Next Page section break</strong> creates a blank pa=
ge.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1271" data-end=3D"1355">Instead of deleting the break, try=
 changing it from <strong data-start=3D"1323" data-end=3D"1336">Next Page</=
strong> to <strong data-start=3D"1340" data-end=3D"1354">Continuous</strong=
>:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"1357" data-end=3D"1594">
<li data-start=3D"1357" data-end=3D"1413">
<p data-start=3D"1360" data-end=3D"1413">Place your cursor <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"1378" data-end=3D"1412">right before the section break</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1414" data-end=3D"1506">
<p data-start=3D"1417" data-end=3D"1506">Go to the <strong data-start=3D"14=
27" data-end=3D"1437">Layout</strong> tab =E2=86=92 click <strong data-star=
t=3D"1450" data-end=3D"1460">Breaks</strong> =E2=86=92 choose <strong data-=
start=3D"1470" data-end=3D"1484">Continuous</strong> under Section Breaks.<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1507" data-end=3D"1594">
<p data-start=3D"1510" data-end=3D"1594">This keeps the section separation =
but removes the forced page break (no blank page).</p>
</li>
</ol>
