<hr data-start=3D"154" data-end=3D"157">
<h3 data-start=3D"159" data-end=3D"215">Alternative Ways to Insert Uppercas=
e Roman Numerals:</h3>
<hr data-start=3D"217" data-end=3D"220">
<h3 data-start=3D"222" data-end=3D"302">Method 1: Use the lowercase Roman n=
umerals and convert to uppercase manually</h3>
<ol data-start=3D"304" data-end=3D"865">
<li data-start=3D"304" data-end=3D"360">
<p data-start=3D"307" data-end=3D"360">Go to <strong data-start=3D"313" dat=
a-end=3D"359">Insert &gt; Page Number &gt; Format Page Numbers</strong>.</p=
>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"361" data-end=3D"416">
<p data-start=3D"364" data-end=3D"416">Select <strong data-start=3D"371" da=
ta-end=3D"388">i, ii, iii...</strong> (lowercase Roman numerals).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"417" data-end=3D"433">
<p data-start=3D"420" data-end=3D"433">Click <strong data-start=3D"426" dat=
a-end=3D"432">OK</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"434" data-end=3D"797">
<p data-start=3D"437" data-end=3D"494">Now, to make them uppercase, you can=
 use <strong data-start=3D"478" data-end=3D"493">Field Codes</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"498" data-end=3D"797">
<li data-start=3D"498" data-end=3D"550">
<p data-start=3D"500" data-end=3D"550">Double-click the page number in the =
header/footer.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"554" data-end=3D"601">
<p data-start=3D"556" data-end=3D"601">Press <strong data-start=3D"562" dat=
a-end=3D"574">Alt + F9</strong> to toggle field code view.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"605" data-end=3D"646">
<p data-start=3D"607" data-end=3D"646">You will see something like <code da=
ta-start=3D"635" data-end=3D"645">{ PAGE }</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"650" data-end=3D"712">
<p data-start=3D"652" data-end=3D"712">Change it to <code data-start=3D"665=
" data-end=3D"684">{ PAGE \* ROMAN }</code> (uppercase Roman numerals).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"716" data-end=3D"758">
<p data-start=3D"718" data-end=3D"758">Press <strong data-start=3D"724" dat=
a-end=3D"736">Alt + F9</strong> again to toggle back.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"762" data-end=3D"797">
<p data-start=3D"764" data-end=3D"797">Press <strong data-start=3D"770" dat=
a-end=3D"776">F9</strong> to update the field.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"798" data-end=3D"865">
<p data-start=3D"801" data-end=3D"865">The page numbers should now display =
as uppercase Roman numerals.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"867" data-end=3D"870">
<h3 data-start=3D"872" data-end=3D"944">Method 2: Insert page numbers manua=
lly with uppercase Roman numerals</h3>
<p data-start=3D"946" data-end=3D"1063">If you only have a few pages, you c=
ould manually type <strong data-start=3D"1000" data-end=3D"1017">I, II, III=
...</strong> but this is not practical for long documents.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1065" data-end=3D"1068">
<h3 data-start=3D"1070" data-end=3D"1086">Explanation:</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1088" data-end=3D"1325">
<li data-start=3D"1088" data-end=3D"1181">
<p data-start=3D"1090" data-end=3D"1181">Word's page numbering formats some=
times only show lowercase Roman numerals in the dropdown.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1182" data-end=3D"1259">
<p data-start=3D"1184" data-end=3D"1259">Using the <strong data-start=3D"11=
94" data-end=3D"1226">field code switch <code data-start=3D"1214" data-end=
=3D"1224">\* ROMAN</code></strong> forces uppercase Roman numerals.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1260" data-end=3D"1325">
